    summary: "Choose the cached object, freshness contract, isolation key, and failure policy explicitly.",
    what: "Memory caching stores application values within one process. A distributed cache shares values through an external service. HTTP response and output caching operate at another boundary: reusable response content under a cache policy. These mechanisms do not provide identical isolation or consistency.",
