    summary: "Keep process health, traffic readiness, and durable work recovery distinct.",
    what: "Liveness asks whether a process should be restarted. Readiness asks whether it should receive new traffic. Startup probes protect slow initialization where supported. Graceful shutdown gives owned operations a bounded opportunity to finish; it cannot guarantee completion after forced termination.",
    why: "A database outage used as a liveness failure can cause every application replica to restart repeatedly. A process that accepts traffic before initialization or is killed mid-job can produce errors even when the new build is correct.",
