    summary: "Translate business language into boundaries and small transactional consistency units.",
    what: "A bounded context gives a model and its language a specific meaning. An aggregate groups state behind a root that protects local invariants. A microservice can contain several aggregates; neither an aggregate nor a database table must become its own network service.",
    why: "A universal Customer or Order model often couples teams with different needs. An excessively large aggregate serializes unrelated changes, while an undersized one can make essential invariants depend on unreliable distributed coordination.",
