    summary: "Limit failure propagation instead of multiplying traffic to an unhealthy dependency.",
    what: "A timeout bounds waiting, a retry repeats eligible work, a circuit breaker temporarily rejects calls after observed failures, and a bulkhead isolates capacity. These mechanisms solve different problems and must fit within an end-to-end deadline.",
    why: "If three layers each make three attempts, one user operation can trigger up to 27 leaf attempts. During an outage, indiscriminate retries consume capacity needed for recovery and can duplicate writes.",
